# AI DocMaster — Startup and Installation Guide

## [1] Environment Setup
1. Configure settings in `.env` (ensure `GEMINI_API_KEY` is set). Refer to `.env.example` for all configurable variables.
2. Start MongoDB local server on port `27017` (or provide a remote connection string like Atlas via `MONGO_URI` in `.env`).
3. Set up python virtual environment and dependencies:
   ```bash
   python -m venv venv
   .\venv\Scripts\activate
   pip install -r backend/requirements.txt
   ```

## [2] Command Matrix (Local Dev vs Production)

| Mode | Backend Server | Frontend Server |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Local Dev** | `python backend/app.py` | `python frontend/serve.py` |
| **Production (Windows)** | `cd backend` <br> `waitress-serve --port=5001 wsgi:app` | Deploy static `frontend/` files behind Nginx |
| **Production (Linux/Mac)** | `cd backend` <br> `gunicorn -w 4 -b 0.0.0.0:5001 wsgi:app` | Deploy static `frontend/` files behind Nginx |

---

## [3] Production Frontend Hosting (Option b)

Since the frontend is composed of separate static HTML/CSS/JS files, it should be deployed using a high-performance static file web server (e.g. Nginx, Apache) or a CDN (e.g. Netlify, Vercel, AWS S3 + CloudFront).

### Sample Nginx Configuration (`/etc/nginx/sites-available/aidocmaster`)
```nginx
server {
    listen 80;
    server_name aidocmaster.example.com;

    # Static frontend files path
    root /var/www/aidocmaster/frontend;
    index index.html;

    location / {
        try_files $uri $uri/ =404;
    }

    # Proxy request API calls to the running backend WSGI server
    location /api/ {
        rewrite ^/api/(.*)$ /$1 break;
        proxy_pass http://127.0.0.1:5001;
        proxy_set_header Host $host;
        proxy_set_header X-Real-IP $remote_addr;
        proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-For $proxy_add_x_forwarded_for;
        proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-Proto $scheme;
    }
}
```

---

## [4] External OS Binary Dependencies

### 1. Poppler (Required for PDF-to-Image conversions)
- Download Poppler binaries for Windows (e.g., from http://blog.alivate.com.au/poppler-windows/ or similar builds).
- Extract and set the path to `bin/` directory under `POPPLER_PATH` in `.env`.

### 2. LibreOffice (Required for Word/Excel/PowerPoint to PDF conversions)
- Download LibreOffice from: https://www.libreoffice.org/download/download-libreoffice/
- Run the installer.
- Add `soffice.exe` parent directory (typically `C:\Program Files\LibreOffice\program`) to your system PATH.

### 3. wkhtmltopdf (Required for HTML-to-PDF conversions)
- Download the installer from: https://wkhtmltopdf.org/downloads.html
- Run the installer and add its `bin` directory (typically `C:\Program Files\wkhtmltopdf\bin`) to your system PATH.

### 4. Tesseract OCR (Required for OCR features)
- Download the Windows installer from: https://github.com/UB-Mannheim/tesseract/wiki
- Run the installer and ensure path matches the `TESSERACT_PATH` configured in `.env`.

